A||||5||btoth||Headlight changing tips?||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||12-15-2001||10:38 PM||||Last time I changed one of my headlights, it turned into a big pain in the neck.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Anyone have any tips to simplify the procedure?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-15-2001||10:52 PM||||in my cave.... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-17-2001||08:27 AM||||Sure.....turn the HL on.  Remove the screws on either side of the black "bezel".  Remove the 4 screws that hold the HL in and replace the HL.  Hope this helps.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||10
Z||000003||honegod||12-17-2001||09:03 AM||||put antisieze on the bulb retaining trim screws, so NEXT time they will come out easy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Springtyme||12-17-2001||10:31 AM||||Get the Xenon Headlight Conversion Kit, it makes everything so much brighter and easier.||||reg||4
Z||000005||btoth||12-17-2001||02:19 PM||||OK, so it went pretty easy this time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Last time there was an incident with the spring...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
